![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

The variable names `sin_vals` and `cos_vals` are misleading. `sin_vals` is used to store the results of `cosf`, and `cos_vals` stores the results of `sinf`. This is confusing and could lead to errors during future maintenance. It would be clearer to name the variables according to the function whose results they store.

```
    float4 cos_vals;
    cos_vals.x = cosf(vals.x);
    cos_vals.y = cosf(vals.y);
    cos_vals.z = cosf(vals.z);
    cos_vals.w = cosf(vals.w);
    *top_half = cos_vals;  // STG.128

    float4 sin_vals;
    sin_vals.x = sinf(vals.x);
    sin_vals.y = sinf(vals.y);
    sin_vals.z = sinf(vals.z);
    sin_vals.w = sinf(vals.w);
    *bottom_half = sin_vals;  // STG.128
```

